/*
 * The C interface of WebRTC.rs's sans-I/O engine (rtci-ffi). MIT OR Apache-2.0.
 *
 * Rules: every function returns an int32_t status (RTCI_OK, RTCI_EMPTY or a negative RTCI_ERR_*);
 * rtci_last_error() describes the last error of the calling thread. Handles are freed by their
 * _free function, returned strings by rtci_string_free(). A rtci_pc handle is not thread-safe:
 * calls on one handle must not overlap. Times are monotonic nanoseconds on the caller's origin.
 * See docs/packaging.md.
 */

